the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for *a case*.
    Merkmal 1 holds for *a case*.
    Merkmal 2 holds for *a case*.
    Merkmal 3 holds for *a case*.
    child *a number* of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for *a case*.
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for *a case*.
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Merkmal 1 is decided for *a case*.
    Merkmal 2 is decided for *a case*.
    Merkmal 3 is decided for *a case*.
    the answer to Merkmal 1 for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Merkmal 1 would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    the answer to Merkmal 2 for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Merkmal 2 would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    the answer to Merkmal 3 for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Merkmal 3 would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r3_6_majority_of_children includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/majority-of-children.ruml".

child 1 of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for a case if
    Merkmal 1 holds for the case.

child 2 of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for a case if
    Merkmal 2 holds for the case.

child 3 of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for a case if
    Merkmal 3 holds for the case.

% Mehr als die Hälfte der ausgewerteten Merkmale muss erfüllt sein
Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for a case if
    Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for the case
    and a number M is the count of each N such that
        child a number N of Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt counts for the case
    and a number K = M * 2
    and K > 3.

Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt holds for a case if
    it is not the case that Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for the case
    and Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt would hold for the case.

Mehrheit der Merkmale erfüllt is decided for a case if
    Merkmal 1 is decided for the case
    and Merkmal 2 is decided for the case
    and Merkmal 3 is decided for the case.

Merkmal 1 holds for a case if
    the answer to Merkmal 1 for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Merkmal 1 holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Merkmal 1 for the case is a truth value
    and Merkmal 1 would hold for the case.

Merkmal 1 is decided for a case if
    the answer to Merkmal 1 for the case is a truth value.

Merkmal 2 holds for a case if
    the answer to Merkmal 2 for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Merkmal 2 holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Merkmal 2 for the case is a truth value
    and Merkmal 2 would hold for the case.

Merkmal 2 is decided for a case if
    the answer to Merkmal 2 for the case is a truth value.

Merkmal 3 holds for a case if
    the answer to Merkmal 3 for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Merkmal 3 holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Merkmal 3 for the case is a truth value
    and Merkmal 3 would hold for the case.

Merkmal 3 is decided for a case if
    the answer to Merkmal 3 for the case is a truth value.

